{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Linking related questions: the build design, version 2 (D694, D695; for council review before code)\n     2\t\n     3\tAlex chose A (D694) and narrowed the first version (D695, \"只连数字题\"): a link joins a **newly opened number question** and an **open\n     4\tnumber question it was shown**, in either reading direction; both are asset questions with five-rung ladders and typed bounds. No\n     5\ttheme, event or same-article pair is linked in this version. A chosen link leaves filing alone (D694 (a)). Version 1 of this document\n     6\twas reviewed in council R round 4 (`codex-r4.md`, NOT READY); each finding is answered below (§10).\n     7\t\n     8\t## 0. Versions and entry points\n     9\t\n    10\t- `poc/config/poc-v119.json`: poc-v118 with `matching.engine` `jev-links` and `rejudging.prompt_version` `judging-v8`; nothing else.\n    11\t- `judging-v8.txt` is a byte copy of `judging-v7.txt`; only the code-built dependency block differs (§3). A request with no dependency is\n    12\t  byte-equal under v7 and v8.\n    13\t- `config.ENGINES` gains `jev-links`. Every place that tests `engine == 'jev'` (`round._match`, `scripts/replay.py`,\n    14\t  `parallel_day.ParallelDay`, `budget_replay.py` defaults) treats `jev-links` as Jev; only `round.run` asks the link questions, and only\n    15\t  under `jev-links`. Existing Jev requests are unchanged (`jev.request_for` holds model, state and questions only).\n    16\t- **A store written by poc-v119 opened by poc-v118:** allowed; v118 writes no link, renders a stored link with today's v7 line, and\n    17\t  filing skips it (filing reads the stored kind, not the configuration). A run is meant to keep one configuration; this is the defined\n    18\t  outcome if it does not.\n    19\t- Pins (`tests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py`): the v7 pins stay; added: `judging-v8.txt`'s sha (equal to v7's), the two new\n    20\t  question builders' output, judging-v8's schema (equal to v7's), and a request-level control: one ledger with a link rendered under v8\n    21\t  (exact text) and under v7 (today's text), and one without a link, byte-equal under both.\n    22\t\n    23\t## 1. Where selection runs: after matching has settled what opens\n    24\t\n    25\tIn `round.run`, under `jev-links` only, a new step **between matching (after the second call) and writing**:\n    26\t1. From `checked.outcomes` take the candidates whose outcome is `new` or `succession`; `identity.batch_plan(handover.candidates,\n    27\t   checked.outcomes)` gives their aliases; one canonical candidate per stored question. A candidate refused or not opened is not asked.\n    28\t2. **Eligible pairs:** the canonical candidate C and each open thesis T on C's list (its search list plus the item's shown questions,\n    29\t   `lists.candidate_lists[C] + shown`, the list its relation questions used), when both are number questions: asset kind, five rungs,\n    30\t   the canonical labels with \"Strongly bullish\" at position 1 (`extraction.normalise_ladder`), and a **typed direction** (below). C's\n    31\t   rungs are taken as the writer will store them (`writing.oriented_like` for a succession). A pair outside this set is not asked.\n    32\t   Same-article pairs are not asked (D695).\n    33\t3. **Stage 1, one Jev job per C:** state = `candidate_state(C)`; per eligible T the `READS` question (§2) with `thesis_text(T)`.\n    34\t4. **Stage 2, one Jev job per C with a passing stage-1 answer:** per such pair, the `SIGN` question with the reader and the read question\n    35\t   fixed (§2).\n    36\t5. **The graph check** (§4) on the stored reading relation plus every proposed link of this article, on stored ids (C is represented by\n    37\t   its canonical candidate id until written).\n    38\t6. The selection is recorded as its own `match_records` row (`call_no` 9: the pairs shown, every answer's choice and probabilities, the\n    39\t   links proposed, the labels, each refusal and correction), never truncated.\n    40\t7. `writing.write` gains an argument `links` (default none: today's behaviour) and writes them (§4).\n    41\t\n    42\t`jev.ask` failures (transport or answer shape) fail the article at the step `matched` as a matching failure does today: resumable, and\n    43\ta resume re-asks only what the archive lacks.\n    44\t\n    45\t## 2. The two questions\n    46\t\n    47\t```\n    48\tREADS (choice), state = CANDIDATE (candidate_state), per THESIS:\n    49\t instructions: \"Should one of these two questions be judged with the other's current conclusion in view? Use only the supplied text. THESIS:\\n\" + thesis_text(T)\n    50\t \"candidate_reads_thesis\": \"the CANDIDATE should be judged with the THESIS's current conclusion in view, because the THESIS's answer bounds or drives the CANDIDATE's: a part read against its whole (one product line's sales against the company's total sales; one region's loans against a bank's total loans), or a quantity read against another it depends on (a bank's net interest income against the central bank's year-end rate)\"\n    51\t \"thesis_reads_candidate\": \"the THESIS should be judged with the CANDIDATE's current conclusion in view, for the same reasons with the roles swapped\"\n    52\t \"neither\": \"neither answer bounds or drives the other: unrelated quantities, or the same quantity for the same period and scope; sharing a company, industry or topic is not enough\"\n    53\t\n    54\tSIGN (choice), state = \"READING QUESTION: \" + (candidate_state(C) or thesis_text(T)), per pair:\n    55\t instructions: \"Suppose the READ QUESTION's answer turned out higher. Which way would that move the most likely answer of the READING QUESTION? Use only the supplied text. READ QUESTION:\\n\" + the other question's text\n    56\t \"together\": \"a higher answer to the READ QUESTION makes a higher answer to the READING QUESTION more likely\"\n    57\t \"opposite\": \"a higher answer to the READ QUESTION makes a lower answer to the READING QUESTION more likely\"\n    58\t \"no_clear_sign\": \"the READ QUESTION only caps or bounds the READING QUESTION without moving its most likely answer, or the supplied text does not show which way it moves it\"\n    59\t```\n    60\t\n    61\tSources: PRD 06 (\"B depending on A means B reads A's conclusion\"; its example \"JPM 2027 net interest income → Fed year-end 2027\n    62\trate\"), D51 (chosen in the matching step), D537 and council R (a part reads its whole), judging-v7 lines 4 and 9 (\"a part cannot exceed\n    63\tits whole\"; \"consistent with the conclusions of the theses it depends on\"). The examples come from banking and from a generic product\n    64\tline; none names a company. Same-quantity-same-period is excluded because such a pair is one question (D248); another period of the\n    65\tsame quantity may be linked. A link with no sign is not written: the existing label vocabulary cannot express it (council R round 2).\n    66\t\n    67\t**Decision rule (code):** Jev's returned `choice` decides, accepted only when its probability is at least 0.5 (`THRESHOLD`, as every Jev\n    68\tanswer in `jev_matching` is read). Stage 1 `neither` or below 0.5: no link. Stage 2 `no_clear_sign` or below 0.5: no link. Every\n    69\toutcome is in the selection record.\n    70\t\n    71\t## 3. What the reader is shown (judging-v8)\n    72\t\n    73\t```\n    74\t- v14 (open; first_is_bullish) How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?: now rung 3 Neutral, judged 2026-07-12\n    75\t    Comparison point stated by that judgement: <reference, or \"not stated\">\n    76\t    The system's forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): <implied_outcome, or \"not stated\">\n    77\t    Reasons (excerpt): <reasons, first 600 characters>\n    78\t```\n    79\tIndented lines start with four spaces and a word, never \"- v\" or \"[\", so neither `evidence_shown_in`, `themes_shown_in` nor a block\n    80\theader can read them. Not judged yet: \"now not judged yet\" and nothing more. `store.current_state` also returns `reference` and\n    81\t`implied_outcome` (no v7 reader prints the whole dictionary). A change of the read question's comparison point alone, with its rung and\n    82\t`changed` unchanged, reaches the reader at the reader's next judgement, not in the same round (the round queues on `changed`, as for\n    83\tevery dependency today).\n    84\t\n    85\t## 4. The graph, the circle correction and the writer\n    86\t\n    87\t- **Graph check (one owner, `links.check_graph`, run at selection and again inside the write):** the reading relation = stored\n    88\t  dependency rows (all kinds) plus the proposed links. A proposed link R reads T is refused if T already reads R through the relation.\n    89\t  In this version every proposed link touches the new question C, so a circle needs C to read some T1 and be read by some T2 with T1\n    90\t  reading T2 already (C → T1 → … → T2 → C).\n    91\t- **Correction (PRD 06: \"Refuse a cycle and ask the model to correct it; persistent cycles follow normal failure handling\"):** for each\n    92\t  proposed link on a circle, one correction request: the stage-1 question for that pair again, its instructions extended with \"Reading\n    93\t  this way would make <R> read itself through <path>; a question cannot read its own conclusion.\" and the offending direction removed\n    94\t  from the criteria. The answer goes through stage 2 and the graph check again. A circle that remains after the correction fails the\n    95\t  article at `matched` (\"persistent cycle\"), resumable, as PRD 06 says.\n    96\t- **Labels (code, §5)** are computed from the rungs as stored, inside the write, after C exists.\n    97\t- **Writer:** a link C reads T is written in step 2 with C's other dependencies; a link T reads C after C is created. Each row: the\n    98\t  article's seq, `direction` = the label, `kind = 'reads'`; T, when it is the reader, is added to the article's `changed` set, so the\n    99\t  day's round judges it after C. The plan is re-checked inside the write transaction (the graph, T still open); a mismatch raises\n   100\t  `WriteConflict` as today (the article fails, resumable).\n   101\t- **Store:** `dependencies.kind` (text). `ensure_writable_columns` adds it with default `''`; every existing row reads `''`.\n   102\t- **Filing:** `store.direct_parents` skips `kind = 'reads'` (D694 (a)); rows with `''` narrow exactly as today. `research_context`\n   103\t  reads dependency rows through an explicit column list (today `select *`), so its output keeps its shape.\n   104\t\n   105\t## 5. The label\n   106\t\n   107\t- **Typed direction** of a ladder (`links.typed_direction`): every rung carries typed bounds; each rung's interval is entirely above the\n   108\t  next rung's (−1, values fall) or entirely below it (+1) for every adjacent pair; anything else is None. Prose is not read (unlike\n   109\t  `matching.ladder_direction`).\n   110\t- **Asset reader R reading T** (both five-rung, Strongly bullish at position 1, so R's favourable end is its first rung): R's favourable\n   111\t  end is its high end when R's direction is −1. T's end favourable to R: `together` → T's high end if R's favourable end is high, else\n   112\t  T's low end; `opposite` → the reverse. Label `first_is_bullish` when that end is T's first rung (T's high end is its first rung when\n   113\t  T's direction is −1), else `last_is_bullish`.\n   114\t- Worked case (old-2 07-10): R = v9 (direction −1), T = v14 (−1), `together` → T's high end = its first rung → `first_is_bullish`.\n   115\t  Changing only the sign, only R's direction, or only T's direction each gives `last_is_bullish`.\n   116\t- Eligibility (§1) already requires both directions decided, so a label is always defined for an asked pair.\n   117\t\n   118\t## 6. Table 1: state × event (C new in this article, T open and shown)\n   119\t\n   120\t| Event | Outcome |\n   121\t|---|---|\n   122\t| matching settles C as `new`/`succession`; the pair is eligible; READS and SIGN pass | link proposed; graph check; written in C's commit; reader judged in that day's round after the read question |\n   123\t| READS `neither` / below 0.5; SIGN `no_clear_sign` / below 0.5 | no link; recorded |\n   124\t| C merges into an existing question, is skipped or not opened, or coalesces with another candidate | not asked, or asked once for the canonical candidate |\n   125\t| a pair not eligible (theme, event, two-rung, untyped or shuffled bounds, same article) | not asked (D695) |\n   126\t| a proposed link closes a circle | one correction request; a remaining circle fails the article at `matched`, resumable |\n   127\t| `jev.ask` fails (transport, answer shape) | the article fails at `matched`, resumable; a resume re-asks what the archive lacks |\n   128\t| the plan no longer fits at write time (T closed in between, a circle) | `WriteConflict`; the article fails, resumable |\n   129\t| a crash after selection and before the write | resume re-runs matching and selection from the archive (no new send) and writes once |\n   130\t| a crash after the write | the link is in the article's commit; a resumed day's round rebuilds its queue (`queued_by_ledger`) |\n   131\t| T's conclusion changes in a round | its reader queued once, after it (`queued_by_change`) |\n   132\t| only T's comparison point changes | the reader sees it at its next judgement (§3) |\n   133\t| T closes | the reader keeps reading T's closing conclusion marked \"closed\" (PRD 06's numeric branch) |\n   134\t| the reader closes | not judged; the row stays as history |\n   135\t| a later article shows C and T again | not asked: neither is new (two open questions are a later version) |\n   136\t| an awaited (waiting) row in the store | this version writes none; a legacy waiting row (`kind ''`) binds through `resolve_waiting` as today |\n   137\t| a second writer | one writer per store (dispatch's single writer); the parallel day prepares extraction requests only and leaves matching, selection and writing to the item's turn |\n   138\t| a v118 run on a v119 store | §0 |\n   139\t| a resume under another configuration | the selection record and every call record carry the config checksum; mixing is §0's defined outcome |\n   140\t\n   141\t## 7. Table 2: value × reader\n   142\t\n   143\t| Value | Readers |\n   144\t|---|---|\n   145\t| `dependencies` row with `kind='reads'` | judging: `topological`, `upstream`, `build_prompt`, `check_answer`, `queued_by_change`, `queued_by_ledger`; `store.would_cycle`, `dependants_of`, `dependencies_of`; `links.check_graph`; the service (`dependencies`, `dependants`), `bundle`, `search` records, `research_context` (explicit columns), the idea route: all read \"R depends on T\". `store.direct_parents` (filing) skips it. |\n   146\t| `kind=''` | every reader as today |\n   147\t| the selection `match_records` row (`call_no` 9) | the trace and the July test's readers; no product reader |\n   148\t| T added to `changed` | `round.changed_views_of_day` → `judge_day` |\n   149\t| `current_state.reference`, `.implied_outcome` | the judging-v8 block only |\n   150\t\n   151\t## 8. Table 3: new path × old checks\n   152\t\n   153\t| Check | Under poc-v119 |\n   154\t|---|---|\n   155\t| no-link requests byte-equal | proved at $0: poc-v119 over old-2's 07-01..07-09 with the link questions answered by a fixed `neither` transport equals the rebuilt v118 prefix (every other request from the archive) |\n   156\t| filing under seed-style rows | unchanged (`kind ''`); the existing test stays green |\n   157\t| filing with a `reads` row | no link removed: re-file old-2's stored readings after seq 148 with the link present (105 shared statements, `filing-exposure.md`) |\n   158\t| `cites_views` only names shown dependencies | unchanged |\n   159\t| dependencies judged first | unchanged |\n   160\t| `matching.check` refusals fail the article | selection runs after it and never adds to its refusals |\n   161\t| D59, the theme block | unchanged |\n   162\t| frozen-piece pins | §0 |\n   163\t\n   164\t## 9. Table 4: prior decisions\n   165\t\n   166\tD51, D368 item 2 (the matching step chooses: a Jev question); D191 point 2 (an existing question gains a link when the read question\n   167\topens); D695 (number questions only, one new); D207, D265, D694 (a) (a link moves no statement); D260 (the reader sees the comparison\n   168\tpoint and the forecast); D248 (same quantity and period is one question); PRD 06 (cycles corrected, then normal failure); D354, D359\n   169\t(new versions); D542's five items: a circle through a waiting link cannot arise (no waiting link is written), closing as table 1,\n   170\ttheme twice and historical readers not reached (no theme link, no resolution row), `last_end` absent.\n   171\t\n   172\t## 10. Round-4 findings and where they are answered\n   173\t\n   174\t1 final identity: §1 steps 1–2. 2 one graph, refusals recorded, PRD 06 correction: §1 step 6, §4. 3 lifecycle and theme boundary:\n   175\tD695, §6. 4 July harness: `TEST-PLAN.md` (archive, sequences, dry run, unexpected links, budget). 5 question texts: §2. 6 typed\n   176\tladders: §5. 7 failure and restart rows: §6. Compatibility (current_state, research_context, mixing, pins, entry points): §0, §3, §4.\n   177\t\n   178\t## 11. Tests (with the code; each names its row)\n   179\t\n   180\t1. `typed_direction` and the label: the worked case, its three mirrors, a shuffled middle, prose-only bounds (None).\n   181\t2. Selection under `jev-links` with a fake Jev transport: eligibility (theme, two-rung, same-article and merge cases not asked);\n   182\t   stage 1 and 2 decisions; the canonical candidate asked once; under `jev` no question asked (mutant: asked).\n   183\t3. Graph and correction: a circle corrected; a persistent circle fails the article; no circle written.\n   184\t4. Writer: T reads C written with `kind='reads'`, T in `changed`; WriteConflict when T closed.\n   185\t5. Filing: `direct_parents` skips `reads` (mutant: it narrows); seed-style rows narrow (existing test).\n   186\t6. judging-v8 block exact text; v7 block byte-equal to today's; no-link request byte-equal under v7 and v8.\n   187\t7. Entry points: `config.load` accepts `jev-links`; `scripts/replay.py` and the parallel day treat it as Jev.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/filing-exposure.md\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild-control.log\nrg -n '\"'^## D69[4-9]'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/filing-exposure.md\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild-control.log\nrg -n '\"'^## D69[4-9]'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# The July test: harness, archive, budget and reading rule (D694 (c); for council review before code)\n     2\t\n     3\t## Starting state ($0, done)\n     4\t`rebuild_control.py` → `rebuild-control.log`: old-2 replayed under poc-v118 from 07-01 to 07-09 with a transport that refuses every\n     5\tsend (`only_objects={'NVDA'}`, the comparison launcher's default): 160 items, 55 judgements, all from the archive; equal to old-2's\n     6\tfinished store up to seq 147 on views, keys, rungs, evidence, links, judgements (rung, reasons, cites, changed, reference, implied\n     7\toutcome, request sha), view switches, successions and dependencies. Each sequence starts from its own copy of this ledger.\n     8\t\n     9\t## Before any send ($0, to be built and run)\n    10\t1. **Prefix compatibility:** poc-v119 over 07-01..07-09 from empty, the link questions answered by a fixed `neither` transport, every\n    11\t   other request from the archive: the ledger equals the rebuilt prefix (no link, every other request byte-equal). This shows that\n    12\t   starting the linked arm from the v118 prefix differs from a v119 run only by links v119 would have proposed before 07-10, which are\n    13\t   then counted from the fixed answers' record (none under `neither`).\n    14\t2. **Dry run:** the whole harness for 07-10..07-12 with a fixed fake transport for every call that would be bought: two control and\n    15\t   two linked dry sequences whose 07-10 answers for v9 and v14 differ (labelled \"DRY-A\", \"DRY-B\"); the 07-11 and 07-12 requests of each\n    16\t   must carry its own previous conclusion; the linked dry sequences must write \"v9 reads v14\" at seq 148 (fixed Jev answers) and show\n    17\t   the judging-v8 block in v9's requests; the control ones must not; every other request must be answered from the archive.\n    18\t3. **The rebuilt requests priced** at published rates (`model.PRICES`) to set the reservation; the reading rule frozen.\n    19\t\n    20\t## The sequences\n    21\tThree linked (poc-v119) and three control (poc-v118), each: its own copy of the prefix ledger; serial path (`replay.run`, no day\n    22\trunner); `only_objects={'NVDA'}`; 07-10 to 07-12.\n    23\t\n    24\t**Archive per sequence (layered):** an overlay archive, new and empty, over a read-only copy of old-2's archive. A judge request for v9\n    25\tor v14 (its user text begins \"Thesis v9 (\" or \"Thesis v14 (\") is looked up in the overlay only, so the stored answer can never answer\n    26\tit: both questions are judged fresh every day (council R round 3). Every other request is looked up in the overlay, then the base.\n    27\tAnswers are recorded in the overlay; a retire acts where the row is.\n    28\t\n    29\t**Transport:** the shared reservation ledger of the comparison runs (`clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py`\n    30\t`SharedLedger`, `BudgetTransport`): before each provider attempt (judge, retry, Jev) its worst case is reserved against one ceiling of\n    31\t**$0.15** for all six sequences, then settled at the actual cost. A refused reservation stops that sequence: inconclusive (council R).\n    32\t\n    33\t**Expected new requests:** the v9 and v14 judge calls, the link questions of the item at seq 148 (linked arm), and a v9 judge call\n    34\ton any day it is queued by a changed v14. **Any other archive miss** (extraction, matching, another question's judgement) stops that\n    35\tsequence and is reported, with one exception declared now: if the linked arm's real selection writes a link besides \"v9 reads v14\"\n    36\t(for example to the stand-alone CPU question v8), the selection is kept, the extra reader's judge requests are bought fresh within the\n    37\tceiling, and the sequence is reported with the extra link. A missing \"v9 reads v14\", or v14 reading v9, is a selection miss.\n    38\t\n    39\t## Reading rule (frozen before the send; council R round 2, `codex-r2.md` §7(b), with round 3)\n    40\t- **A. Comparable answers:** both 07-12 answers give a FY2027 forecast in USD for their own quantity (a range by its stated ends);\n    41\t  quarters recorded where both give comparable figures; a missing annual figure leaves reconciliation untested.\n    42\t- **B. Arithmetic and sources:** reported figures keep their amount and scope; the arithmetic follows from the stated inputs within\n    43\t  rounding; each assumption that materially sizes the result is disclosed and supported by the material available that day; a linked\n    44\t  forecast is treated as a forecast with assumptions.\n    45\t- **C. Room for the rest:** the high end of the Data Center forecast is at least $6B below the low end of the company forecast (the Q1\n    46\t  floor: $81.6B total minus $75.25B Data Center); each comparable quarter keeps the segment within the total.\n    47\t- **D. The link did the work (linked arm):** matching chose \"v9 reads v14\", the writer committed it at seq 148, and v9 used v14's\n    48\t  forecast in its calculation or as a stated bound; delivery and use of the Bloomberg-compiled $393B (e195) recorded separately; a\n    49\t  mention or citation alone earns no credit.\n    50\t- **Pass:** at least two of three linked sequences meet A–D; at most one control meets A–C; no first-attempt refusal added and no new\n    51\t  material grounding error on either question across 07-10..07-12 (relabelling a system forecast as a market estimate, or treating\n    52\t  $393B as a Data Center consensus, is one). **Inconclusive:** two or more controls reconcile, fewer than two comparable sequences in\n    53\t  either arm, or a ceiling stop. **Fail:** a new material error, an added refusal, fewer than two correct link selections, or any other\n    54\t  miss. Failures take precedence.\n    55\t- **Readers:** Claude's marks written first, then a fresh blind Codex reader on the six sequences under shuffled labels, the key outside\n    56\t  the repository; every sequence reported.\n     1\t# Filing exposure under literal D265 (old-2, $0; 2026-11-21)\n     2\t\n     3\tCounted on old-2's stored reading answers (`handovers`, seq >= 148, the item that opened total revenue v14): **105** statements were\n     4\tlinked by the reading step to both v9 (Data Center FY2027) and v14 (total revenue FY2027). With a link \"v9 reads v14\" read as a\n     5\thierarchy (D265 literally, `extraction.narrowest_links`), each would keep v9 only. Among them, seq 185: \"NVIDIA reported record FY2027\n     6\tfirst-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year\" and \"NVIDIA management guided FY2027 Q2 revenue to approximately $91\n     7\tbillion\": total revenue's own figure and guidance (D207: \"company-wide figure questions take only their own figures, guidance and\n     8\tmanagement statements\"). A first-order count: a replay under the literal rule would diverge from the archive at the first moved link,\n     9\tso the exact loss is not replayable at $0. Under D694 (a) (`kind = 'reads'` skipped by `store.direct_parents`) none moves.\n     1\t2026-07-01 | items  13 extracted  13 merged  0 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence   5 new views  3 judged   3 changed   3 closed 0 | open views 3 | day $0.00 total $0.00 calls 0\n     2\t2026-07-02 | items  19 extracted  17 merged  2 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence  23 new views  1 judged   3 changed   3 closed 0 | open views 4 | day $0.00 total $0.00 calls 0\n     3\t2026-07-03 | items  10 extracted   9 merged  1 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence   4 new views  0 judged   2 changed   0 closed 0 | open views 4 | day $0.00 total $0.00 calls 0\n     4\t2026-07-04 | items   6 extracted   5 merged  1 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence   7 new views  2 judged   6 changed   5 closed 0 | open views 6 | day $0.00 total $0.00 calls 0\n     5\t2026-07-05 | items  10 extracted   7 merged  3 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence  13 new views  2 judged   8 changed   7 closed 0 | open views 8 | day $0.00 total $0.00 calls 0\n     6\t2026-07-06 | items  29 extracted  25 merged  4 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence  51 new views  1 judged   9 changed   7 closed 0 | open views 9 | day $0.00 total $0.00 calls 0\n     7\t2026-07-07 | items  22 extracted  22 merged  0 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence  31 new views  0 judged   9 changed   6 closed 0 | open views 9 | day $0.00 total $0.00 calls 0\n     8\t2026-07-08 | items  27 extracted  26 merged  1 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence  31 new views  3 judged  10 changed   8 closed 0 | open views 12 | day $0.00 total $0.00 calls 0\n     9\t2026-07-09 | items  24 extracted  23 merged  1 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence  29 new views  1 judged   5 changed   3 closed 0 | open views 13 | day $0.00 total $0.00 calls 0\n    10\ttotals: {'items': 160, 'extracted': 147, 'skipped': 0, 'merged': 13, 'not_processed': 0, 'returned': 0, 'failed': 0, 'evidence': 194, 'new_views': 13, 'judged': 55, 'changed': 42, 'closed': 0}\n    11\tlast completed seq at 2026-07-09 147\n    12\tviews: rebuilt 13 stored 13 equal\n    13\tview_keys: rebuilt 13 stored 13 equal\n    14\tevidence: rebuilt 194 stored 194 equal\n    15\tevidence_links: rebuilt 232 stored 232 equal\n    16\tjudgements: rebuilt 55 stored 55 equal\n    17\trungs: rebuilt 44 stored 44 equal\n    18\tview_switches: rebuilt 13 stored 13 equal\n    19\tsuccessions: rebuilt 0 stored 0 equal\n    20\tdependencies: rebuilt 0 stored 0 equal\n10439:## D694 · 2026-11-21 · Alex chooses A: links leave filing alone; new matching and judging versions open for linking; the July test after the council passes the $0 proof\n10454:## D695 · 2026-11-21 · Alex narrows the first linking version to number questions, one of them newly opened\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^class BudgetTransport|def (wrap|__call__|openai|jev|reserve|settle|mark|run)'\"' clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py\nnl -ba clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '155,422p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '39,107p;245,286p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/jev.py | sed -n '23,49p;57,112p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^class BudgetTransport|def (wrap|__call__|openai|jev|reserve|settle|mark|run)'\"' clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py\nnl -ba clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '155,422p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '39,107p;245,286p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/jev.py | sed -n '23,49p;57,112p'\"","aggregated_output":"131:    def reserve(self, amount):\n153:    def settle(self, reserved, actual, kind='llm', tokens=None):\n256:def jev_estimate(request):\n262:class BudgetTransport:\n268:    def __call__(self, *args):\n   155\t        request never costs nothing, and a failed attempt is charged its reservation. `kind` (llm, jev, embeddings) and the reported\n   156\t        `tokens` go to the attempt line only.\"\"\"\n   157\t        _LIVE.depth = max(0, getattr(_LIVE, 'depth', 0) - 1)\n   158\t        if not isinstance(actual, (int, float)) or isinstance(actual, bool) or not math.isfinite(actual) or actual <= 0:\n   159\t            actual = reserved\n   160\t        with self._locked() as state:\n   161\t            state['reserved'] = max(0.0, state['reserved'] - reserved)\n   162\t            state['spent'] += actual\n   163\t            if actual > reserved + 1e-12:\n   164\t                state['overrun'] = True\n   165\t                if not state.get('stopped'):\n   166\t                    state['stopped'], state['stop_reason'] = True, 'overrun'\n   167\t        self._note({'kind': kind, 'reserved': reserved, 'charged': actual, **({'tokens': tokens} if tokens is not None else {})})\n   168\t\n   169\t    def stop_if_a_launcher_is_gone(self):\n   170\t        \"\"\"Under the ledger's lock: a registered launcher whose lock no process holds died without removing its entry; the ledger is\n   171\t        stopped. A relaunch calls this before it takes its own lock, so its new lock never makes a stale entry look alive; the stop gate\n   172\t        calls it before every send. Returns the state after the check.\"\"\"\n   173\t        with self._locked() as state:\n   174\t            if not state.get('stopped'):\n   175\t                for label, lock_path in sorted((state.get('launchers') or {}).items()):\n   176\t                    if lock_is_free(lock_path):\n   177\t                        state['stopped'], state['stop_reason'] = True, f'the launcher of {label} is gone'\n   178\t                        break\n   179\t            return dict(state)\n   180\t\n   181\t    def claim_launcher(self, label, lock_handle):\n   182\t        \"\"\"One step under the ledger's lock (council mo, D449): stop the ledger if any registered launcher's lock is free; try the\n   183\t        launcher's own lock without blocking (False: another launch of this label is running); if this label is still registered once\n   184\t        its lock is held, the previous launcher died without removing its entry, so the ledger stops; then register. The stop gate's\n   185\t        probe takes the same lock, so no send can see a stale entry as alive while a new launcher takes its lock.\"\"\"\n   186\t        with self._locked() as state:\n   187\t            launchers = state.setdefault('launchers', {})\n   188\t            if not state.get('stopped'):\n   189\t                for other, lock_path in sorted(launchers.items()):\n   190\t                    if lock_is_free(lock_path):\n   191\t                        state['stopped'], state['stop_reason'] = True, f'the launcher of {other} is gone'\n   192\t                        break\n   193\t            try:\n   194\t                fcntl.flock(lock_handle, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)\n   195\t            except BlockingIOError:\n   196\t                return False\n   197\t            if label in launchers and not state.get('stopped'):\n   198\t                state['stopped'], state['stop_reason'] = True, f'the launcher of {label} is gone'\n   199\t            launchers[label] = os.path.abspath(lock_handle.name)\n   200\t            return True\n   201\t\n   202\t    def register_launcher(self, label, lock_path):\n   203\t        \"\"\"Register a launcher's lock path (tests and proofs; a launcher uses `claim_launcher`).\"\"\"\n   204\t        with self._locked() as state:\n   205\t            state.setdefault('launchers', {})[label] = str(lock_path)\n   206\t\n   207\t    def remove_launcher(self, label):\n   208\t        \"\"\"Called by a launcher on a normal end, before it releases its lock.\"\"\"\n   209\t        with self._locked() as state:\n   210\t            (state.get('launchers') or {}).pop(label, None)\n   211\t\n   212\t    def stop(self, reason):\n   213\t        \"\"\"A stop any component records: every later reservation is refused.\"\"\"\n   214\t        with self._locked() as state:\n   215\t            if not state.get('stopped'):\n   216\t                state['stopped'], state['stop_reason'] = True, reason\n   217\t\n   218\t    def read(self):\n   219\t        with open(self.lock_path, 'a+') as lock:\n   220\t            fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\n   221\t            try:\n   222\t                return json.loads(self.path.read_text())\n   223\t            finally:\n   224\t                fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n   225\t\n   226\t\n   227\tdef llm_estimate(request):\n   228\t    price_in, price_out = model.PRICES[request['model']]\n   229\t    cap = request.get('max_completion_tokens', request.get('max_tokens'))\n   230\t    if isinstance(cap, bool) or not isinstance(cap, int) or cap <= 0:\n   231\t        raise model.TransportError('request without a positive output cap: refused by the budget')\n   232\t    tokens_in = 2 * len(json.dumps(request).encode('utf-8')) + 4096\n   233\t    return (tokens_in * price_in + cap * price_out) / 1e6\n   234\t\n   235\t\n   236\tdef whole(count):\n   237\t    return isinstance(count, int) and not isinstance(count, bool) and count >= 0\n   238\t\n   239\t\n   240\tdef llm_cost(response, request):\n   241\t    \"\"\"The answer's cost by `model.call`'s formula; None (settled at the reservation) unless the counts are whole, nonnegative numbers\n   242\t    with some input.\"\"\"\n   243\t    usage = response.get('usage') if isinstance(response, dict) else None\n   244\t    if not isinstance(usage, dict):\n   245\t        return None\n   246\t    tokens_in, tokens_out = usage.get('prompt_tokens'), usage.get('completion_tokens')\n   247\t    details = usage.get('prompt_tokens_details') or {}\n   248\t    cached = (details.get('cached_tokens') or 0) if isinstance(details, dict) else None\n   249\t    if not (whole(tokens_in) and whole(tokens_out) and whole(cached)) or tokens_in == 0:\n   250\t        return None\n   251\t    price_in, price_out = model.PRICES[request['model']]\n   252\t    cached = min(tokens_in, cached)\n   253\t    return (tokens_in - cached) / 1e6 * price_in + cached / 1e6 * price_in * model.CACHED_INPUT_SHARE + tokens_out / 1e6 * price_out\n   254\t\n   255\t\n   256\tdef jev_estimate(request):\n   257\t    price_in, _ = model.PRICES[request['model']]\n   258\t    tokens_in = 2 * len(json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False).encode('utf-8')) + 4096\n   259\t    return jev.ATTEMPTS * tokens_in * price_in / 1e6\n   260\t\n   261\t\n   262\tclass BudgetTransport:\n   263\t    \"\"\"Called as production calls a transport: (provider, request) for a language model, (request,) for Jev.\"\"\"\n   264\t\n   265\t    def __init__(self, ledger, sleep=time.sleep):\n   266\t        self.ledger, self.sleep = ledger, sleep\n   267\t\n   268\t    def __call__(self, *args):\n   269\t        if len(args) == 1:\n   270\t            return self._jev(args[0])\n   271\t        provider, request = args\n   272\t        for attempt in range(3):\n   273\t            estimate = llm_estimate(request)\n   274\t            if not self.ledger.reserve(estimate):\n   275\t                raise model.TransportError('the shared budget ceiling would be passed: not sent')\n   276\t            try:\n   277\t                response = model.openai_transport(provider, request, max_attempts=1)\n   278\t            except model.TransportError as error:\n   279\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   280\t                status = getattr(error, 'http_status', None)\n   281\t                if status in CLIENT_ERRORS or attempt == 2 or (status is not None and status != 429 and status < 500):\n   282\t                    raise\n   283\t                self.sleep(5 * (attempt + 1))\n   284\t                continue\n   285\t            except Exception:\n   286\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   287\t                raise\n   288\t            cost = llm_cost(response, request)\n   289\t            self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate if cost is None else cost)\n   290\t            return response\n   291\t        raise model.TransportError('no answer after three attempts')\n   292\t\n   293\t    def _jev(self, request):\n   294\t        estimate = jev_estimate(request)\n   295\t        if not self.ledger.reserve(estimate):\n   296\t            raise model.TransportError('the shared budget ceiling would be passed: not sent')\n   297\t        try:\n   298\t            response = jev.transport(request)\n   299\t        except Exception:\n   300\t            self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate, kind='jev')\n   301\t            raise\n   302\t        usage = response.get('usage') if isinstance(response, dict) else None\n   303\t        tokens = usage.get('input_tokens') if isinstance(usage, dict) else None\n   304\t        if isinstance(tokens, int) and not isinstance(tokens, bool) and tokens > 0:\n   305\t            # an unanswered attempt inside jev.transport was the same request, so each of the three is billed at most this input;\n   306\t            # the whole charge is settled, so a charge above the reservation sets the overrun flag\n   307\t            actual = jev.ATTEMPTS * tokens * model.PRICES[request['model']][0] / 1e6\n   308\t        else:\n   309\t            actual = estimate                       # usage missing, invalid, or zero for a nonempty request: the whole reservation\n   310\t        self.ledger.settle(estimate, actual, kind='jev', tokens=tokens if isinstance(tokens, int) else None)\n   311\t        return response\n   312\t\n   313\t\n   314\tdef main():\n   315\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n   316\t    parser.add_argument('--init-ledger')\n   317\t    parser.add_argument('--ceiling', type=float)\n   318\t    parser.add_argument('--ledger')\n   319\t    parser.add_argument('--from', dest='from_day')\n   320\t    parser.add_argument('--until', dest='until_day')\n   321\t    parser.add_argument('--testdb', default=str(ROOT / 'poc/data/items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite'))\n   322\t    parser.add_argument('--views')\n   323\t    parser.add_argument('--archive')\n   324\t    parser.add_argument('--config', default=str(ROOT / 'poc/config/poc-v118.json'))\n   325\t    parser.add_argument('--universe', default=str(ROOT / 'poc/universe.json'))\n   326\t    parser.add_argument('--only', default='NVDA')\n   327\t    parser.add_argument('--cap', type=float, default=None)\n   328\t    parser.add_argument('--workers', type=int, default=16)\n   329\t    parser.add_argument('--jev-workers', type=int, default=None)\n   330\t    args = parser.parse_args()\n   331\t    if args.init_ledger:\n   332\t        if Path(args.init_ledger).exists():\n   333\t            raise SystemExit('ledger exists: refused (a new ledger needs a new path)')\n   334\t        SharedLedger.init(args.init_ledger, args.ceiling)\n   335\t        print('ledger written:', args.init_ledger, 'ceiling', args.ceiling)\n   336\t        return\n   337\t    for name in ('ledger', 'from_day', 'until_day', 'views', 'archive'):\n   338\t        if not getattr(args, name):\n   339\t            raise SystemExit(f'--{name.replace(\"_day\", \"\")} is required')\n   340\t    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.views), exist_ok=True)\n   341\t    log_path = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(args.views), 'replay.log')\n   342\t\n   343\t    def log(*parts):\n   344\t        line = ' '.join(str(p) for p in parts)\n   345\t        print(line, flush=True)\n   346\t        with open(log_path, 'a', encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n   347\t            handle.write(line + '\\n')\n   348\t\n   349\t    cfg = config.load(args.config)\n   350\t    if cfg.baseline is not None:\n   351\t        raise SystemExit(f'config {cfg.version} uses the retired seeded-question baseline: refused')\n   352\t    import importlib.util\n   353\t    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('scripts_replay', ROOT / 'scripts/replay.py')\n   354\t    scripts_replay = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n   355\t    spec.loader.exec_module(scripts_replay)\n   356\t    scripts_replay.refuse_seeded_ledger(args.views)          # the same refusal scripts/replay.py makes\n   357\t    uni = universe.load(args.universe)\n   358\t    archive = model.Archive(args.archive)\n   359\t    ledger = SharedLedger(args.ledger)\n   360\t    install_stop_gate(ledger)                              # Jev's internal retries read the run's stop too (council mo R1)\n   361\t    transport = BudgetTransport(ledger)\n   362\t    jev_workers = args.jev_workers if args.jev_workers is not None else (8 if cfg.matching.engine == 'jev' else 1)\n   363\t    day_runner = parallel_day.ParallelDay(os.path.abspath(args.testdb), os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(args.views)), 'manifests'),\n   364\t                                          extraction_workers=args.workers, jev_workers=jev_workers) if args.workers > 1 else None\n   365\t    log(f'--- budgeted replay {args.from_day}..{args.until_day} config {cfg.version}/{cfg.checksum} provider {cfg.provider} universe {uni.version} '\n   366\t        f'workers {args.workers}; ledger {args.ledger} {ledger.read()}')\n   367\t    totals = replay.run(testdb_path=args.testdb, views_path=args.views, archive=archive, cfg=cfg, universe=uni,\n   368\t                        from_day=args.from_day, until_day=args.until_day, spend_cap_usd=args.cap, log=log,\n   369\t                        only_objects=set(args.only.split(',')) if args.only else None, transport=transport, day_runner=day_runner)\n   370\t    log('totals:', totals)\n   371\t    log('ledger:', ledger.read())\n   372\t\n   373\t\n   374\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   375\t    main()\n    39\tSCHEMA_SQL = \"\"\"\n    40\tcreate table if not exists model_calls (\n    41\t  call_id integer primary key autoincrement, purpose text, config_version text, config_checksum text, model text,\n    42\t  request_sha256 text unique, request_json text, response_json text, answer_json text, prompt_chars integer,\n    43\t  input_tokens integer, output_tokens integer, cost_usd real, seconds real, created_at text\n    44\t);\n    45\tcreate index if not exists model_calls_sha on model_calls(request_sha256);\n    46\t\"\"\"\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\tclass SchemaError(ValueError):\n    50\t    pass\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\tclass TransportError(RuntimeError):\n    54\t    pass\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\t@dataclasses.dataclass\n    58\tclass Answer:\n    59\t    data: dict\n    60\t    call_id: int\n    61\t    request_sha256: str\n    62\t    cached: bool\n    63\t    prompt_chars: int\n    64\t    input_tokens: int\n    65\t    output_tokens: int\n    66\t    cost_usd: float\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\tclass Archive:\n    70\t    \"\"\"Shared by the extraction worker threads: one connection, every access under a lock.\"\"\"\n    71\t\n    72\t    def __init__(self, path):\n    73\t        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(path)), exist_ok=True)\n    74\t        self.conn = sqlite3.connect(path, check_same_thread=False)\n    75\t        self.conn.executescript(SCHEMA_SQL)\n    76\t        import threading\n    77\t        self.lock = threading.Lock()\n    78\t\n    79\t    def lookup(self, sha):\n    80\t        with self.lock:\n    81\t            return self.conn.execute('select call_id, answer_json, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens from model_calls where request_sha256=?', (sha,)).fetchone()\n    82\t\n    83\t    def record(self, **fields):\n    84\t        \"\"\"One row per distinct request; a second identical request recorded at the same moment (two threads, or a\n    85\t        failed answer repeated within the same second) keeps the first row's id instead of failing.\"\"\"\n    86\t        columns = list(fields)\n    87\t        with self.lock:\n    88\t            cursor = self.conn.execute(f'insert or ignore into model_calls ({\",\".join(columns)}) values ({\",\".join(\"?\" * len(columns))})',\n    89\t                                       [fields[c] for c in columns])\n    90\t            self.conn.commit()\n    91\t            if cursor.rowcount == 0:\n    92\t                return self.conn.execute('select call_id from model_calls where request_sha256=?', (fields['request_sha256'],)).fetchone()[0]\n    93\t            return cursor.lastrowid\n    94\t\n    95\t    def retire(self, call_id):\n    96\t        \"\"\"A code check refused this answer: the row stays for the record, but no later identical request is answered with it\n    97\t        (the same shape as a schema-refused or malformed row, whose hash carries a suffix).\"\"\"\n    98\t        with self.lock:\n    99\t            self.conn.execute(\"update model_calls set request_sha256 = request_sha256 || ':refused:' || ? where call_id=? and request_sha256 not like '%:refused:%'\",\n   100\t                              (uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], call_id))\n   101\t            self.conn.commit()\n   102\t\n   103\t    def totals(self):\n   104\t        with self.lock:\n   105\t            return self.conn.execute('select count(*), coalesce(sum(cost_usd),0), coalesce(sum(input_tokens),0), coalesce(sum(output_tokens),0) from model_calls').fetchone()\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   245\tdef request_identity(request):\n   246\t    \"\"\"The exact serialized request and its archive key, shared by callers and validation.\"\"\"\n   247\t    encoded = json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False)\n   248\t    return encoded, hashlib.sha256(encoded.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()\n   249\t\n   250\t\n   251\tdef call(archive, cfg, setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, purpose, *, transport=None):\n   252\t    provider = cfg.provider\n   253\t    request = build_request(setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, provider)\n   254\t    request_json, sha = request_identity(request)\n   255\t    hit = archive.lookup(sha)\n   256\t    prompt_chars = len(system) + len(user)\n   257\t    if hit:\n   258\t        call_id, answer_json, _, input_tokens, output_tokens = hit\n   259\t        return Answer(json.loads(answer_json), call_id, sha, True, prompt_chars, input_tokens or 0, output_tokens or 0, 0.0)\n   260\t    started = time.time()\n   261\t    response = (transport or openai_transport)(provider, request)\n   262\t    seconds = round(time.time() - started, 1)\n   263\t    try:\n   264\t        content = response['choices'][0]['message']['content']\n   265\t        data = json.loads(content)\n   266\t    except (KeyError, IndexError, TypeError, json.JSONDecodeError) as error:\n   267\t        archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n   268\t                       request_sha256=sha + ':malformed:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n   269\t                       response_json=json.dumps(response)[:200000], answer_json=None, prompt_chars=prompt_chars,\n   270\t                       input_tokens=0, output_tokens=0, cost_usd=0.0, seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   271\t        raise SchemaError(f'malformed answer: {error}')\n   272\t    errors = check_schema(data, schema)\n   273\t    usage = response.get('usage') or {}\n   274\t    input_tokens = int(usage.get('prompt_tokens') or 0)\n   275\t    output_tokens = int(usage.get('completion_tokens') or 0)\n   276\t    cached_tokens = min(input_tokens, int((usage.get('prompt_tokens_details') or {}).get('cached_tokens') or 0))\n   277\t    price_in, price_out = PRICES.get(setting.model, (0.0, 0.0))\n   278\t    cost = round((input_tokens - cached_tokens) / 1e6 * price_in + cached_tokens / 1e6 * price_in * CACHED_INPUT_SHARE + output_tokens / 1e6 * price_out, 6)\n   279\t    call_id = archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n   280\t                             request_sha256=sha if not errors else sha + ':schema:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n   281\t                             response_json=json.dumps(response)[:200000], answer_json=json.dumps(data, ensure_ascii=False),\n   282\t                             prompt_chars=prompt_chars, input_tokens=input_tokens, output_tokens=output_tokens, cost_usd=cost,\n   283\t                             seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   284\t    if errors:\n   285\t        raise SchemaError('; '.join(errors[:5]))\n   286\t    return Answer(data, call_id, sha, False, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost)\n    23\t        return os.environ[KEY_NAME]\n    24\t    with open(model.CREDENTIALS, encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n    25\t        return json.load(handle)[KEY_NAME]\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\tdef transport(request, timeout=60):\n    29\t    \"\"\"POST the request; up to three attempts, pausing before each retry, on a rate-limit or overload status or a\n    30\t    connection that fails without a reply; any other failure is a TransportError. The body is the same sorted text the\n    31\t    archive digests, so a cache hit is byte-identical to what was sent.\"\"\"\n    32\t    body = json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False).encode('utf-8')\n    33\t    key = _key()\n    34\t    for attempt in range(ATTEMPTS):\n    35\t        req = urllib.request.Request(ENDPOINT, body, {'Authorization': 'Bearer ' + key, 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Accept': 'application/json'})\n    36\t        try:\n    37\t            with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as response:\n    38\t                raw = response.read()\n    39\t            break\n    40\t        except urllib.error.HTTPError as error:\n    41\t            if error.code not in RETRY_STATUSES or attempt == ATTEMPTS - 1:\n    42\t                raise model.TransportError(f'Jev HTTP {error.code}') from None\n    43\t        except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError, http.client.HTTPException) as error:   # a dropped or truncated reply\n    44\t            if attempt == ATTEMPTS - 1:\n    45\t                raise model.TransportError(f'Jev transport failed: {type(error).__name__}') from None\n    46\t        time.sleep(2 * (attempt + 1))\n    47\t    if key.encode('utf-8') in raw:\n    48\t        raise model.TransportError('Jev response echoed the credential; not archived')\n    49\t    return json.loads(raw.decode('utf-8'))\n    57\tdef validate(answers, questions):\n    58\t    \"\"\"The answers of a response against the request's questions; a list of problems.\"\"\"\n    59\t    problems = []\n    60\t    if not isinstance(answers, dict) or set(answers) != set(questions):\n    61\t        return ['answer set differs from the questions asked']\n    62\t    for qid, question in questions.items():\n    63\t        answer = answers[qid]\n    64\t        if not isinstance(answer, dict) or answer.get('type') != question['type']:\n    65\t            problems.append(f'{qid}: answer type mismatch')\n    66\t            continue\n    67\t        if question['type'] == 'noul':\n    68\t            if not isinstance(answer.get('noul'), (int, float)) or not 0 <= answer['noul'] <= 1:\n    69\t                problems.append(f'{qid}: noul out of range')\n    70\t        elif question['type'] == 'choice':\n    71\t            probabilities = answer.get('probabilities')\n    72\t            if answer.get('choice') not in question['criteria'] or not isinstance(probabilities, dict) or set(probabilities) != set(question['criteria']):\n    73\t                problems.append(f'{qid}: choice or probabilities do not match the criteria')\n    74\t            elif any(not isinstance(v, (int, float)) or isinstance(v, bool) or not 0 <= v <= 1 for v in probabilities.values()) \\\n    75\t                    or abs(sum(probabilities.values()) - 1) > 0.005 * len(probabilities) + 1e-9:\n    76\t                problems.append(f'{qid}: probabilities are not a distribution')\n    77\t            elif probabilities[answer['choice']] < max(probabilities.values()) - ROUNDING - 1e-9:\n    78\t                problems.append(f'{qid}: choice is not the most probable option')\n    79\t    return problems\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\tdef request_for(setting, state, questions):\n    83\t    \"\"\"The complete Jev request used both for dispatch and in-flight identity.\"\"\"\n    84\t    return {'model': setting.model, 'state': state, 'questions': questions}\n    85\t\n    86\t\n    87\tdef ask(archive, cfg, setting, state, questions, purpose, *, transport=None):\n    88\t    \"\"\"One Jev request, archived; returns model.Answer whose data is the `answers` map.\"\"\"\n    89\t    request = request_for(setting, state, questions)\n    90\t    request_json, sha = model.request_identity(request)\n    91\t    prompt_chars = len(request_json)\n    92\t    hit = archive.lookup(sha)\n    93\t    if hit:\n    94\t        call_id, answer_json, _, input_tokens, output_tokens = hit\n    95\t        return model.Answer(json.loads(answer_json), call_id, sha, True, prompt_chars, input_tokens or 0, output_tokens or 0, 0.0)\n    96\t    started = time.time()\n    97\t    response = (transport or globals()['transport'])(request)\n    98\t    seconds = round(time.time() - started, 2)\n    99\t    answers = response.get('answers') if isinstance(response, dict) else None\n   100\t    problems = validate(answers, questions)\n   101\t    usage = response.get('usage') or {} if isinstance(response, dict) else {}\n   102\t    input_tokens, output_tokens = int(usage.get('input_tokens') or 0), int(usage.get('output_tokens') or 0)\n   103\t    price_in, _ = model.PRICES.get(setting.model, (0.0, 0.0))\n   104\t    cost = round(input_tokens / 1e6 * price_in, 6)\n   105\t    call_id = archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n   106\t                             request_sha256=sha if not problems else sha + ':schema:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n   107\t                             response_json=json.dumps(response, ensure_ascii=False)[:200000], answer_json=json.dumps(answers, ensure_ascii=False) if answers is not None else None,\n   108\t                             prompt_chars=prompt_chars, input_tokens=input_tokens, output_tokens=output_tokens, cost_usd=cost,\n   109\t                             seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   110\t    if problems:\n   111\t        raise model.SchemaError('; '.join(problems[:5]))\n   112\t    return model.Answer(answers, call_id, sha, False, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/views/round.py | sed -n '27,61p;97,166p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/views/writing.py | sed -n '49,82p;112,156p;175,206p'\nrg -n 'view_key|EVENT_MEASURES|check_bounds|normalise_ladder|changed' src/hivemind/{extraction,vocabulary}.py\nnl -ba src/hivemind/dispatch.py | sed -n '23,58p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/live_lock.py | sed -n '48,85p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/views/round.py | sed -n '27,61p;97,166p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/views/writing.py | sed -n '49,82p;112,156p;175,206p'\nrg -n 'view_key|EVENT_MEASURES|check_bounds|normalise_ladder|changed' src/hivemind/{extraction,vocabulary}.py\nnl -ba src/hivemind/dispatch.py | sed -n '23,58p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/live_lock.py | sed -n '48,85p'\"","aggregated_output":"    27\tdef _fail(conn, item, seq, result, step, kind, detail, pool_key):\n    28\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, step, 'failed', detail[:300])\n    29\t    store.pool(conn, kind, pool_key, {'input_id': item['input_id'], 'error': detail[:300]}, seq)\n    30\t    result.failed = detail[:200]\n    31\t    conn.commit()\n    32\t    return result\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\tdef _match(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, result, candidates, evidence, lists, shown, *, extra_views=(), call_offset=0, transport=None, workers=1):\n    36\t    \"\"\"One matching call with one retry on a refused check. Returns Checked, or None after marking the failure.\"\"\"\n    37\t    note = ''\n    38\t    checked = None\n    39\t    engine = jev_matching if cfg.matching.engine == 'jev' else matching      # Jev answers once; a retry would be the same answer\n    40\t    for attempt in range(1 if engine is jev_matching else 2):\n    41\t        try:\n    42\t            options = {'workers': workers, 'llm_transport': transport} if engine is jev_matching else {}     # the collision judge sends with the caller's transport too\n    43\t            answer = engine.decide(archive, cfg, conn, item, candidates, evidence, lists, shown, extra_views=extra_views, retry_note=note, transport=transport, **options)\n    44\t        except Exception as error:\n    45\t            _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'matched', 'matching_failed', 'matching: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\n    46\t            return None\n    47\t        result.cost += answer.cost_usd\n    48\t        result.cached_calls += int(answer.cached)\n    49\t        checked = matching.check(conn, universe, answer.data, candidates, evidence, lists, shown)\n    50\t        shown_record = {'candidates': lists.candidate_lists, 'evidence': {f'{k[0]}|{k[1]}': v for k, v in lists.evidence_lists.items()}}\n    51\t        if getattr(answer, 'request_records', None):\n    52\t            shown_record['requests'] = answer.request_records\n    53\t        store.insert(conn, 'match_records', seq=seq, input_id=item['input_id'], call_no=call_offset + attempt + 1,\n    54\t                     shown_json=json.dumps(shown_record),\n    55\t                     request_sha256=answer.request_sha256, call_id=answer.call_id, decisions_json=json.dumps(answer.data, ensure_ascii=False),\n    56\t                     checks_json=json.dumps({'refusals': checked.refusals, 'not_opened': checked.not_opened, 'notes': checked.notes}, ensure_ascii=False), written_json=None)\n    57\t        if not checked.refusals:\n    58\t            return checked\n    59\t        note = '；'.join(checked.refusals)\n    60\t    _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'matched', 'matching_refused_twice', 'matching refused twice: ' + note, item['category'])\n    61\t    return None\n    97\tdef run(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, *, resume_from=None, transport=None, log=print, extractor=None, matching_workers=1):\n    98\t    result = RoundResult(item['input_id'])\n    99\t    if resume_from in ('judged', 'handed_over'):       # written already; judging is the day's step\n   100\t        dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'handed_over', 'ok', 'resumed')\n   101\t        conn.commit()\n   102\t        return result\n   103\t    objects = [o['value'] for o in item.get('object_identifiers') or [] if universe.has(o['value'])]\n   104\t    shown = extraction.shown_views(conn, cfg, item, objects)\n   105\t    # extraction (or its stored handover on resume)\n   106\t    handover = None\n   107\t    if resume_from and resume_from != 'extracted':\n   108\t        row = conn.execute('select handover_json from handovers where input_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (item['input_id'],)).fetchone()\n   109\t        if row:\n   110\t            saved = vocabulary.extraction_answer(json.loads(row['handover_json']))          # a handover saved by a Chinese version reads in the canonical vocabulary\n   111\t            handover = extraction.Handover(saved['evidence'], saved['candidates'], saved['dropped'], 0, '', True, 0.0, saved.get('new_groups') or [])\n   112\t    if handover is None:\n   113\t        try:\n   114\t            handover = (extractor or extraction.extract)(archive, cfg, item, item['text'], shown, universe, transport=transport)\n   115\t        except Exception as error:\n   116\t            return _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'extracted', 'extraction_failed', 'extraction: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\n   117\t        result.cost += handover.cost_usd\n   118\t        result.cached_calls += int(handover.cached)\n   119\t        store.insert(conn, 'handovers', input_id=item['input_id'], seq=seq,\n   120\t                     handover_json=json.dumps({'evidence': handover.evidence, 'candidates': handover.candidates, 'dropped': handover.dropped, 'new_groups': handover.new_groups}, ensure_ascii=False))\n   121\t        dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'extracted', 'ok', f'{len(handover.evidence)} evidence, {len(handover.candidates)} candidates, {len(handover.dropped)} dropped')\n   122\t        conn.commit()\n   123\t    result.evidence, result.candidates, result.dropped = len(handover.evidence), len(handover.candidates), len(handover.dropped)\n   124\t    if not handover.evidence and not handover.candidates:\n   125\t        dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'handed_over', 'ok', 'nothing to match')\n   126\t        conn.commit()\n   127\t        return result\n   128\t    # first matching call: the candidates and the evidence linked straight to existing views\n   129\t    lists = matching.build_lists(conn, handover, shown, cfg.search_top_n)\n   130\t    checked = _match(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, result, handover.candidates, handover.evidence, lists, shown, transport=transport, workers=matching_workers)\n   131\t    if checked is None:\n   132\t        return result\n   133\t    # second call: evidence linked to candidates that attached to an existing view, compared under that view\n   134\t    second_pass = {}\n   135\t    pending = []\n   136\t    for e in handover.evidence:\n   137\t        for link in e['links']:\n   138\t            outcome = checked.outcomes.get(link)\n   139\t            if outcome and outcome[0] == 'merge':\n   140\t                pending.append((e, outcome[1]))\n   141\t    if pending:\n   142\t        lists2 = matching.Lists({}, {(e['id'], view_id): matching.rank_evidence(conn, view_id, e['one_line'], cfg.search_top_n) for e, view_id in pending})\n   143\t        evidence2, seen = [], set()\n   144\t        for e, view_id in pending:\n   145\t            if e['id'] not in seen:\n   146\t                evidence2.append(dict(e, links=[v for x, v in pending if x['id'] == e['id']]))\n   147\t                seen.add(e['id'])\n   148\t        checked2 = _match(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, result, [], evidence2, lists2, [], extra_views=sorted({v for _, v in pending}),\n   149\t                          call_offset=2, transport=transport, workers=matching_workers)\n   150\t        if checked2 is None:\n   151\t            return result\n   152\t        second_pass = checked2.evidence\n   153\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'matched', 'ok', f'{len(checked.outcomes)} candidates placed')\n   154\t    # write, and record what changed in the same commit (a resume at 'judged' reads it)\n   155\t    try:\n   156\t        written = writing.write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass)\n   157\t    except Exception as error:\n   158\t        return _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'written', 'writing_failed', 'writing: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\n   159\t    result.new_views = len(set(written.new_views.values()))\n   160\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'written', 'ok', json.dumps({'changed': sorted(written.changed_views), 'new': written.new_views, 'notes': written.notes[:20]}, ensure_ascii=False))\n   161\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'handed_over', 'ok', '')\n   162\t    conn.commit()\n   163\t    return result\n    49\tdef resolve_waiting(conn, new_view_id, seq, changed):\n    50\t    \"\"\"A new view on a chain satisfies dependencies waiting for its year on that chain.\"\"\"\n    51\t    v = store.view(conn, new_view_id)\n    52\t    chain = {new_view_id}\n    53\t    frontier = [new_view_id]\n    54\t    while frontier:\n    55\t        current = frontier.pop()\n    56\t        for row in conn.execute('select succeeds from successions where view_id=?', (current,)):\n    57\t            if row['succeeds'] not in chain:\n    58\t                chain.add(row['succeeds'])\n    59\t                frontier.append(row['succeeds'])\n    60\t    for dep in conn.execute('select * from dependencies where wait_year=? and wait_chain_view_id is not null', (v['year'],)):\n    61\t        if dep['wait_chain_view_id'] in chain:\n    62\t            already = conn.execute('select 1 from dependency_resolutions where dependency_id=?', (dep['dependency_id'],)).fetchone()\n    63\t            if not already and not store.would_cycle(conn, dep['view_id'], new_view_id):\n    64\t                store.insert(conn, 'dependency_resolutions', dependency_id=dep['dependency_id'], resolved_to=new_view_id, reason='created', seq=seq)\n    65\t                changed.add(dep['view_id'])\n    66\t\n    67\t\n    68\tdef object_id_of(universe, candidate):\n    69\t    return universe.resolve(candidate['object']) or candidate['object']\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\tdef oriented_like(c, previous, notes):\n    73\t    \"\"\"06-views: a successor's ladder keeps the predecessor's direction. A numeric ladder written the other way round (rung 1 the\n    74\t    lowest band where the predecessor's rung 1 is the highest) is the same ladder; it is stored reversed, rungs with their\n    75\t    labels and bounds, so positions mean the same along the chain. Undecidable pairs are stored as written.\"\"\"\n    76\t    from .matching import ladder_direction\n    77\t    before, after = (ladder_direction(previous) if previous else None), ladder_direction(c['rungs'])\n    78\t    if before is not None and after is not None and before != after:\n    79\t        notes.append(f'candidate {c[\"id\"]}: successor ladder reversed to the predecessor\\'s direction')\n    80\t        return dict(c, rungs=list(reversed(c['rungs'])))\n    81\t    return c\n    82\t\n   112\tdef write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass):\n   113\t    \"\"\"Write atomically within the caller's transaction; the caller commits the completion marker with it.\"\"\"\n   114\t    if not conn.in_transaction:\n   115\t        conn.execute('begin immediate')\n   116\t    conn.execute('savepoint view_write')\n   117\t    try:\n   118\t        store.ensure_writable_columns(conn)\n   119\t        result = _write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass)\n   120\t    except Exception:\n   121\t        conn.execute('rollback to view_write')\n   122\t        conn.execute('release view_write')\n   123\t        raise\n   124\t    conn.execute('release view_write')\n   125\t    return result\n   126\t\n   127\t\n   128\tdef _write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass):\n   129\t    \"\"\"second_pass: {(handover evidence id, view_id): (outcome, target_evidence_id, said_day)} for candidate-linked\n   130\t    evidence compared after the candidates' destinations were known (new views' evidence is simply new).\"\"\"\n   131\t    changed, notes, new_views, evidence_ids = set(), [], {}, {}\n   132\t    candidate_ids = {c['id'] for c in handover.candidates}\n   133\t    aliases, problems = identity.batch_plan(handover.candidates, checked.outcomes)\n   134\t    if problems:\n   135\t        raise WriteConflict('; '.join(problems))\n   136\t    created = {}\n   137\t    # 1. new views, themes first\n   138\t    order = sorted(handover.candidates, key=lambda c: 0 if c['kind'] == 'theme' else 1)\n   139\t    for c in order:\n   140\t        outcome, target, deps = checked.outcomes.get(c['id'], ('skip', None, []))\n   141\t        if outcome not in ('new', 'succession'):\n   142\t            continue\n   143\t        canonical = aliases[c['id']]\n   144\t        if canonical in created:\n   145\t            new_views[c['id']] = created[canonical]\n   146\t            continue\n   147\t        if store.exact_key_views(conn, c):\n   148\t            raise WriteConflict(f'candidate {c[\"id\"]}: existing exact identity requires matching')\n   149\t        object_id = universe.resolve(c['object'])\n   150\t        if outcome == 'succession' and target:\n   151\t            c = oriented_like(c, store.rungs_of(conn, target), notes)\n   152\t        view_id = _create_view(conn, c, object_id, universe.kind(object_id), seq, item, universe)\n   153\t        new_views[c['id']] = view_id\n   154\t        created[canonical] = view_id\n   155\t        if outcome == 'succession' and target:\n   156\t            store.insert(conn, 'successions', view_id=view_id, succeeds=target, seq=seq)\n   175\t    # 2. dependencies of the new views (candidate ids resolve to the views just created)\n   176\t    dependencies_written = set()\n   177\t    for c in order:\n   178\t        outcome, target, deps = checked.outcomes.get(c['id'], ('skip', None, []))\n   179\t        if c['id'] not in new_views:\n   180\t            continue\n   181\t        view_id = new_views[c['id']]\n   182\t        for dep in deps:\n   183\t            depends_on = dep['view_id']\n   184\t            if depends_on in new_views:\n   185\t                depends_on = new_views[depends_on]\n   186\t            elif depends_on in candidate_ids:\n   187\t                notes.append(f'dependency {view_id} -> candidate {depends_on} dropped: that candidate was not opened')\n   188\t                continue\n   189\t            if depends_on and store.would_cycle(conn, view_id, depends_on):\n   190\t                notes.append(f'dependency {view_id} -> {depends_on} dropped: cycle')\n   191\t                continue\n   192\t            chain = dep['wait_chain_view_id']\n   193\t            if chain in new_views:\n   194\t                chain = new_views[chain]\n   195\t            wait_year = dep['wait_year']\n   196\t            if wait_year and chain and hasattr(universe, 'canonical_year'):          # the chain's object decides the spelling (FY2027 or 2026)\n   197\t                chain_view = store.view(conn, chain)\n   198\t                wait_year = universe.canonical_year(chain_view['object_id'] if chain_view else object_id_of(universe, c), wait_year)\n   199\t            edge = (view_id, depends_on, chain, wait_year, dep['direction'])\n   200\t            if edge in dependencies_written:\n   201\t                continue\n   202\t            dependencies_written.add(edge)\n   203\t            store.insert(conn, 'dependencies', view_id=view_id, depends_on=depends_on, wait_chain_view_id=chain, wait_year=wait_year,\n   204\t                         direction=dep['direction'], seq=seq)\n   205\t        resolve_waiting(conn, view_id, seq, changed)\n   206\t    # 3. where each piece of evidence goes\nsrc/hivemind/vocabulary.py:5:never rewritten, and an unknown value passes through unchanged so that the schema or the code check that owns the\nsrc/hivemind/vocabulary.py:29:    \"\"\"The canonical value of a closed field: a legacy value converted, a canonical one kept, anything else unchanged.\"\"\"\nsrc/hivemind/extraction.py:48:    return [dict(v, key=store.view_key(conn, v['view_id']) or {},\nsrc/hivemind/extraction.py:214:# stored quote is always verbatim. Any added, changed or reordered word or number, a dropped +/− on a number or a changed currency\nsrc/hivemind/extraction.py:269:    near = _near_run(quote_tokens, source_tokens, subject_names)   # D266: a function word or the company's own name changed, added or dropped\nsrc/hivemind/extraction.py:283:# A changed month, party, product or number, a paraphrase, and two names swapped are refused as before (D236's tests hold).\nsrc/hivemind/extraction.py:413:    Strongly bullish (the model often orders a revenue ladder by rising value) is the same ladder; normalise_ladder\nsrc/hivemind/extraction.py:426:def normalise_ladder(rungs, kind):\nsrc/hivemind/extraction.py:493:def check_bounds(rungs):\nsrc/hivemind/extraction.py:624:        c = dict(c, rungs=normalise_ladder(c['rungs'], c['kind']))\nsrc/hivemind/extraction.py:645:            problem = check_bounds(c['rungs'])\n    23\tdef route(conn, item, universe):\n    24\t    missing = [field for field in REQUIRED if not item.get(field)]\n    25\t    if missing:\n    26\t        store.pool(conn, 'incomplete_item', ','.join(missing), {'input_id': item.get('input_id'), 'missing': missing}, 0)\n    27\t        return Route('returned', reason=f'missing {missing}')\n    28\t    input_id = item['input_id']\n    29\t    if store.is_processed(conn, input_id):\n    30\t        return Route('skipped', reason='already processed')\n    31\t    last = store.last_step(conn, input_id)\n    32\t    if last and last['step'] in STEPS and last['sequence_no']:\n    33\t        # unfinished work keeps its sequence number: after an ok step it continues at the next step, after a\n    34\t        # failed step it retries that step (06-views: 失败从失败的那一步重试)\n    35\t        position = STEPS.index(last['step'])\n    36\t        resume_from = STEPS[position + 1] if last['result'] == 'ok' else last['step']\n    37\t        return Route('extract', sequence_no=last['sequence_no'], resume_from=resume_from, reason='resuming')\n    38\t    if item.get('copy_of'):\n    39\t        return Route('merged', reason=f'copy of {item[\"copy_of\"]}')\n    40\t    if item.get('supersedes'):\n    41\t        store.pool(conn, 'correction_not_supported', item['supersedes'], {'input_id': input_id}, 0)\n    42\t        return Route('not_processed', reason='correction (supersedes) not supported in the POC')\n    43\t    category = item['category']\n    44\t    objects = [o['value'] for o in item.get('object_identifiers') or [] if universe.has(o['value'])]\n    45\t    if not objects:\n    46\t        return Route('not_processed', reason='no object on the research list')\n    47\t    if not any(universe.watches(o, category) for o in objects):\n    48\t        return Route('not_processed', reason=f'category {category} not watched for {objects}')\n    49\t    # the sequence number is taken in arrival order and written at once, so two items routed before either is\n    50\t    # processed (a whole day is routed first, then run) never share a number\n    51\t    sequence_no = store.next_sequence(conn)\n    52\t    store.mark_step(conn, input_id, sequence_no, 'dispatched', 'ok', '', item.get('publication_day'), time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n    53\t    conn.commit()\n    54\t    return Route('extract', sequence_no=sequence_no, reason='')\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\tdef mark(conn, item, sequence_no, step, result='ok', reason=''):\n    58\t    store.mark_step(conn, item['input_id'], sequence_no, step, result, reason, item.get('publication_day'), time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n    48\t\n    49\tclass Held:\n    50\t    \"\"\"A held lock: the store's real path and identity, the lock file's path, descriptor and inode.\"\"\"\n    51\t\n    52\t    def __init__(self, real_path, identity, lock_path, descriptor):\n    53\t        self.real_path, self.identity, self.lock_path, self.descriptor = real_path, identity, lock_path, descriptor\n    54\t        self.lock_inode = os.fstat(descriptor).st_ino\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\tdef acquire(store_path):\n    58\t    \"\"\"The store's lock, without waiting: refused when another process holds it.\"\"\"\n    59\t    real, identity = own_path(store_path)\n    60\t    lock_path = os.path.join(lock_folder(), f'{identity[0]}-{identity[1]}.writer.lock')\n    61\t    descriptor = os.open(lock_path, os.O_CREAT | os.O_RDWR, 0o600)\n    62\t    try:\n    63\t        fcntl.flock(descriptor, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)\n    64\t    except BlockingIOError:\n    65\t        os.close(descriptor)\n    66\t        raise LockRefused(f'{real} is being written (its lock is held): read a snapshot of it instead (scripts/snapshot_store.py)') from None\n    67\t    held = Held(real, identity, lock_path, descriptor)\n    68\t    try:\n    69\t        verify(held)\n    70\t    except BaseException:\n    71\t        release(held)\n    72\t        raise\n    73\t    return held\n    74\t\n    75\t\n    76\tdef verify(held):\n    77\t    \"\"\"The store's path still names the locked file with no other hard link, and the lock file's path still names the locked lock\n    78\t    file; otherwise `PathChanged`.\"\"\"\n    79\t    try:\n    80\t        status = os.stat(held.real_path)\n    81\t    except FileNotFoundError:\n    82\t        raise PathChanged(f'{held.real_path} no longer exists') from None\n    83\t    if os.path.realpath(held.real_path) != held.real_path or (status.st_dev, status.st_ino) != held.identity:\n    84\t        raise PathChanged(f'{held.real_path} no longer names the locked store')\n    85\t    if status.st_nlink > 1:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
