{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10439,10487p'\nrg -n 'writing\\\\._write\\\\b|writing\\\\.write\\\\b|match_records|def (lookup|record|retire|totals|prepare)|BudgetTransport|jev_transport' src scripts tests clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py --glob '*.py'\nnl -ba scripts/preflight.py | sed -n '220,268p'\"","aggregated_output":" 10439\t## D694 · 2026-11-21 · Alex chooses A: links leave filing alone; new matching and judging versions open for linking; the July test after the council passes the $0 proof\n 10440\t\n 10441\t- **Alex's words** (2026-11-21), replying to the three choices of D693: \"A\". The options were:\n 10442\t  - **A**, recommended: (a) a chosen reading link leaves evidence filing alone (D265 applies only to a stated hierarchy); (b) open new\n 10443\t    matching and judging versions for the shared mechanism (both opening orders; the first test accepts only the existing-reader /\n 10444\t    new-target case); (c) after the $0 proof has passed the council, the July comparison (old-2, 07-10 to 07-12, three linked and three\n 10445\t    control sequences, both questions fresh, pass rule `dependency-design/codex-r2.md` §7(b)), cap $0.15, estimate $0.06–0.07;\n 10446\t  - **B**, the code and the $0 proof only, asking again before the paid test;\n 10447\t  - **C**, not now.\n 10448\t- **Decided (Alex):** A. poc-v118 stays the product and the control; the linking version is a new configuration. The sourced-reference\n 10449\t  change is not opened (it returns after the July measurement, D693).\n 10450\t- **Next:** the $0 work of D693 in order (tables and request audit; the July control rebuilt by request identity and filing replayed;\n 10451\t  real checks and writer with fixed answers for both orders and the listed events; built requests inspected, rule frozen, cap set),\n 10452\t  then the council on the proof, then the send.\n 10453\t\n 10454\t## D695 · 2026-11-21 · Alex narrows the first linking version to number questions, one of them newly opened\n 10455\t\n 10456\t- **The question** (after council R round 4, `docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r4.md`, NOT READY: the\n 10457\t  design's blanket exclusion of theme links narrowed the agreed lifecycle, and the full scope — themes shown once with the link's\n 10458\t  direction, a theme reading an asset, closed events read as historical until a successor, two questions opened by one article — needs\n 10459\t  more design rounds): \"连题的第一版，范围要多大？\" Options: only number questions (recommended): link two five-rung number questions\n 10460\t  of the asset kind, one of them newly opened; themes already reach every asset question through the theme block (D191, D195);\n 10461\t  yes/no event questions and two questions opened by the same article wait for a later version. Or the agreed design in full.\n 10462\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-21): \"只连数字题 (推荐)\".\n 10463\t- **Decided (Alex):** the first linking version links only a newly opened number question and an open number question it was shown,\n 10464\t  in either reading direction (both five-rung asset ladders with typed bounds). No theme, event or same-article pair is linked in this\n 10465\t  version; each is a later version Alex opens. D694 otherwise stands.\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:4:and the day's judging): `BudgetTransport` sends each request exactly as the production transports do, after reserving its worst cost\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:262:class BudgetTransport:\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:361:    transport = BudgetTransport(ledger)\nscripts/preflight.py:231:        for rec in conn.execute('select input_id, call_no, shown_json, decisions_json, request_sha256 from match_records order by id'):\nscripts/review_english_run.py:120:    for r in conn.execute('select checks_json from match_records'):\nsrc/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:5:`writing.write` run unchanged: `merge` when a listed open thesis is the same quantity or event, `succession` when a\ntests/test_groups.py:54:    written = writing.write(conn, UNIVERSE, 1, ITEM, first, matching.Checked({'c1': ('new', None, []), 'c2': ('new', None, [])}, {}, [], {}), {})\ntests/test_groups.py:64:    written2 = writing.write(conn, UNIVERSE, 2, ITEM, later, matching.Checked({'c3': ('new', None, []), 'c4': ('merge', dc, [])}, {}, [], {}), {})\ntests/test_groups.py:81:    def recording(*parameters):\ntests/test_groups.py:104:    written = writing.write(conn, UNIVERSE, 1, ITEM, lines_only, matching.Checked({'c1': ('new', None, []), 'c2': ('new', None, [])}, {}, [], {}), {})\ntests/test_groups.py:113:    written2 = writing.write(conn, UNIVERSE, 2, ITEM, second, matching.Checked({'c3': ('new', None, []), 'c4': ('new', None, []), 'c5': ('new', None, [])}, {}, [], {}), {})\ntests/test_groups.py:137:    written = writing.write(conn, UNIVERSE, 1, ITEM, first, matching.Checked({'c1': ('new', None, []), 'c2': ('new', None, [])}, {}, [], {}), {})\ntests/test_groups.py:147:    written2 = writing.write(conn, UNIVERSE, 2, ITEM, second, matching.Checked({'c3': ('new', None, [])}, {}, [], {}), {})\ntests/test_groups.py:154:    written_line = writing.write(conn, UNIVERSE, 5, ITEM, extraction.Handover([dict(EVIDENCE[0], id='e9', links=['c9'])], [line], [], 0, '', False, 0.0, []),\ntests/test_groups.py:161:    written3 = writing.write(conn, UNIVERSE, 3, dict(ITEM, object_identifiers=[{'value': 'AMZN'}]), third, matching.Checked({'c4': ('new', None, [])}, {}, [], {}), {})\nsrc/hivemind/views/round.py:53:        store.insert(conn, 'match_records', seq=seq, input_id=item['input_id'], call_no=call_offset + attempt + 1,\nsrc/hivemind/views/round.py:156:        written = writing.write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass)\nscripts/hivemind_api.py:177:        def prepare(db):\nscripts/re