{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"The revised scope resolves the theme and event questions. I found two concrete gaps in the new plan: Jev has one shared state per job, and the proposed archive receives only a request hash at lookup. Both affect whether the July test can run as written."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY. D695 resolves the theme, event and same-article scope questions. The revised design still has three build blockers: the sign request cannot be batched as written, the cycle check omits reachable links, and the archive cannot guarantee fresh July answers through its current interface.** The expanded sequence-147 comparison and the 105-item filing replay give the build a concrete starting state and filing check. [D695](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10454) · [Rebuild log](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild-control.log:10) · [Filing exposure](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/filing-exposure.md:1)\n\n## Build blockers\n\n**1. `SIGN` has one shared state per job, but the design gives it a different state for each pair.** Section 1 says one sign job per candidate. Section 2 makes the reading question the job’s state. If two existing questions both read the same new candidate, those pairs need different states. Jev accepts one `state` for the entire request. Keep the candidate in the shared state and identify the reading question and the question being read in each pair’s instructions. Exercise one job containing both reading directions. [Design §1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:23) · [Design §2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:45) · [Jev request shape](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/jev.py:82)\n\nThe revised `READS` and `SIGN` ask the right questions for July. The expected answers are `thesis_reads_candidate` and, if the reported segment mix is a defensible guide, `together`. The returned `choice` and its own probability now give a clear decision rule. Finish the prompt audit against D695: the central-bank-rate example is a theme-side pair this version cannot ask, and §6 calls for examples of each class, including `opposite`, `no_clear_sign` and `neither`. Keep relevance and sign with the model. Code should enforce eligibility and translate the chosen sign. [July selection case](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/selection-census.md:59) · [Jev answer validation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/jev.py:57) · [AGENTS §6](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:226)\n\n**2. The graph must include all openings and any waiting links that become active in the same write.** Section 4 assumes a cycle needs one new question and a path already stored between two existing questions. One article can open two questions. Four otherwise eligible new-to-existing links can form `C1 → T1 → C2 → T2 → C1` without any stored path. Table 1 also permits legacy waits to bind through `resolve_waiting`, while Table 4 says a waiting cycle cannot arise. A legacy wait for a new successor can become the return path for a proposed reading link. Today `resolve_waiting` can leave it unbound without recording the cycle. [Design §4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:85) · [Design Table 1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:118) · [Waiting resolver](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:49)\n\nThe proposed correction **does** follow PRD 06 if it runs on the complete graph. Use the same checker before writing and inside the savepoint. Include any waits that would bind, or enforce a writer admission rule that makes them unreachable. Record the rejected direction and path, replace each corrected pair’s original answer, and recheck the full set. A remaining cycle fails the item at `matched`. Add $0 cases for the four-link cycle and the waiting-successor cycle. [PRD 06](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/06-views.md:133) · [Write savepoint](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:112)\n\n**3. The July archive contract cannot work through `lookup(sha)` as described.** Both `model.call` and `jev.ask` check the archive before transport, passing just the hash. `retire` receives just an integer ID. Two independent SQLite archives can return the same ID, and the read-only base cannot retire a refusal. “Retire where the row is” is therefore ambiguous. The simpler design is one writable scratch archive per sequence, preserving existing IDs for replayed calls and excluding stored target-judge answers from exact lookup. Alternatively, specify request-aware routing before lookup, a single ID namespace, and how retirement masks a base hit. Prove at $0 that an exact old target request goes to the fresh transport, an unrelated exact hit does not, and a refused answer cannot reappear. [Test plan §The sequences](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:20) · [Archive API](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:69) · [Model lookup](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:251) · [Jev lookup](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/jev.py:87)\n\n## Other changes needed before build\n\n**4. The placement in `round.run` is correct. Complete the checked plan and its record.** Run selection after the evidence-only second match returns and before the `matched` success marker. Use the first call’s `checked.outcomes` and lists. A keyword-only `proposed_links=None` on `writing.write` can preserve the existing six-argument callers. Pass the canonical endpoints, direction and sign into the savepoint, resolve the new ID there, and compute the final label from the stored rungs. Specify whether the earlier selection record holds a predicted label or whether the committed write records the final label. A valid selector response and a committed link are different events. [Round entry point](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/round.py:128) · [Writer interface](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:112) · [Existing direct writer test](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_identity_repair.py:110)\n\n`call_no=9` has readers beyond the July test. Preflight treats every number above 2 as evidence comparison, and the trace uses the same grouping. Give the selection record an explicit type and define its handling in both places. Record the config checksum and individual call IDs and hashes, including partial successes before a transport failure. The current `match_records` schema has no checksum column. Pin either the exact stored metadata shape or a separate record with its readers listed. [Match record schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:29) · [Preflight](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/preflight.py:220) · [Trace grouping](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/trace_items.py:138)\n\n**5. The label formula works, but eligibility still excludes a reachable numeric successor.** The worked case and the three mirrors are correct under the assumed labels. `oriented_like` can reverse the whole ladder, including its labels, putting **Strongly bullish** last in the stored successor. D695 requires a five-rung asset number ladder with typed bounds. It does not require the favourable end to be first. Accept the canonical label order or its reverse, then derive the favourable end from the final stored labels. Use the candidate’s measure and the existing question’s stored key to exclude event measures explicitly. Define how typed intervals handle touching boundaries, open outer ends, and inverted or empty intervals. [Design §5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:105) · [Successor orientation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:72) · [Event measures](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/identity.py:8)\n\n**6. The July dry run, extra links and budget need three corrections.**\n\n- **Check requests that actually run.** Old-2 has no Data Center judgement on July 11. Assert that the control does not invent one, and exercise both outcomes in the linked dry run: a changed total queues Data Center, and an unchanged total leaves it unqueued when it has no other trigger. Every subsequent request that runs must carry its own sequence’s last accepted answer. The fixed-`neither` prefix test proves compatibility on a no-link prefix. It cannot count what live v119 would have selected there. [Test plan §Before any send](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:9) · [Daily judging queue](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:300)\n- **Keep the paid set to the two questions.** The exception that buys an extra reader’s judgement changes the comparison agreed in rounds 3–4. Keep and report any genuine extra selection, but stop on an unrelated archive miss. Register how an extra link that changes a scored request affects the result before sending. A missing or reversed intended link remains a selection miss. [Test plan’s extra-link exception](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:33) · [Council R test contract](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/RESULT.md:49)\n- **Use the budget transport’s actual behaviour.** It accepts both provider signatures. For Luna it reserves per attempt. For Jev it reserves the full internal retry bundle and settles conservatively at up to `ATTEMPTS ×` reported usage, or at the reservation if usage is unavailable. Use the existing stop gate for internal retries. Check the shared ledger after replay stops so a cap refusal becomes **inconclusive for the comparison**, even when `round.run` reports it as a matching or judging failure. [Budget transport](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:262) · [Stop gate](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:69) · [Round failure handling](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/round.py:27)\n\n**7. Finish the restart and judging rows.** A checksum in a call record does not enforce same-configuration resume. Distinguish a version switch between completed days from a restart midway through a day. Define the outcome for changed input, changed configuration, paid calls still in flight, and a second process writing the same store. Dispatch allocates a sequence before the item savepoint and has no cross-process writer exclusion. Reuse an enforced per-store writer boundary or explicitly refuse that entry path. In judging, qualify “reader judged after the read question” by eligibility. A new target without evidence stays unjudged. For a comparison-point-only change, exercise both `changed=true` and `changed=false`; the latter reaches the reader at its next judgement under the existing rule. [Design Table 1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:118) · [Dispatch](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/dispatch.py:23) · [Store writer lock](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/live_lock.py:57) · [Judge eligibility and propagation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:300)\n\nThe v7 compatibility plan, new request pins, legacy filing default and explicit research-context projection address the round-4 findings. In the renderer test, include a multiline comparison point, forecast and reasons, so every physical continuation line stays inside its block. Keep the existing v7 byte-equality control. [Version and pin plan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:8) · [Renderer plan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:71)\n\nRevise the sign job, validate the complete graph including reachable waits, specify archive routing and retirement, and close the record, ladder, restart and July budget cases above. The before-build review is read-only. **NOT READY TO BUILD.**"}}
